# ASCII source (no Unicode punctuation)

Do not put Unicode punctuation or symbols in source trees this agent edits.

- Use ASCII \-\ instead of em dash / en dash (U+2014 / U+2013).
- Use ASCII \->\ / \<-\ instead of arrow glyphs (U+2192 / U+2190).
- Use ASCII \...\ instead of ellipsis (U+2026).
- Keep comments, scripts (.ps1, .sh), CMake, and commit messages free of non-ASCII.
- Still write files as UTF-8 without BOM; byte-verify (no NULs) to avoid the Cursor UTF-16LE bug.
- Exception: fixtures/tests that deliberately exercise non-ASCII data (e.g. UTF-8 name conversion).
